.TH ZERODDS-SPY 1 "May 2026" "ZeroDDS 1.0.0-rc.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zerodds-spy \- subscribe to a DDS topic and dump samples
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-spy
[\fBsubscribe\fR]
\fB\-t\fR \fITOPIC\fR
[\fB\-d\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR \fICOUNT\fR]
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDUR\fR]
[\fB\-x\fR \fIBYTES\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-spy
starts a DCPS runtime, subscribes to the given
.B \-\-topic
as untyped raw bytes, and prints metadata plus an optional hex snippet
for every incoming sample.
.PP
The
.B subscribe
sub-command is implicit when the first argument is a flag — the two
forms below are equivalent:
.PP
.RS
zerodds-spy subscribe -t Foo
.br
zerodds-spy -t Foo
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIID\fR
DDS Domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fINAME\fR
Topic name to subscribe (REQUIRED).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-count " " \fIN\fR
Stop after N samples. Default: unlimited.
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fIDUR\fR
Stop after duration: \fI5\fR, \fI30s\fR, \fI2m\fR, \fI1h\fR.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-hex " " \fIBYTES\fR
First BYTES of the payload as hex (0 disables). Default: 32.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
CLI parse error.
.TP
.B 3
DDS or I/O error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-record (1),
.BR zerodds-snitch (1),
.BR zerodds-pcap (1)
